From: Johan Alvarado <contact@c127.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: realtek: add RTL8367S SerDes PCS support

Integrate the upstream RTL8367S PCS implementation, HSGMII support, and the RTL8367D SerDes path as one coherent PCS implementation.

The SGMII and HSGMII PCS implementations were originally authored by
Johan Alvarado and merged into net-next as:

Link: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/netdev/net-next.git/commit/?id=0b577e2fe06c
Link: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/netdev/net-next.git/commit/?id=987137345f33
Link: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/netdev/net-next.git/commit/?id=fcaf2221b970

[Fabiano: combine and backport the upstream SGMII/HSGMII series to Linux
6.12; add the RTL8367D SDS13 programming model, 2500base-x mapping and
MR80X-specific opt-in integration while retaining the generic upstream
path for other switches.]

Signed-off-by: Johan Alvarado <contact@c127.dev>
Signed-off-by: Fabiano Tassotti <fabianotassotti@gmail.com>

